              "name": "Eyebrow",
              "fill": "$color-interactive",
              "content": "NEW CONCEPT · BATCH 41 · AUTOMATIC FOLLOW-UP CARD · APPROVED B · 2026-10-21",
              "lineHeight": 1.35,
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-small",
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": 0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "WWO0s",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$color-heading",
              "content": "Automatic follow-up card",
              "lineHeight": 1.35,
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-jumbo",
              "fontWeight": "700",
              "letterSpacing": -0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Ko4gN",
              "name": "Lead",
              "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Approved by Jafar 2026-10-21: B · Next message first (A refined rows deleted). automation/InquiryAutomationCard, in the side column of a Request and of a website chat in the Inbox. It shows the automatic reply a website inquiry gets: whether the next message is waiting, paused and why, stuck, finished, or stopped and why, and lets staff Pause, Resume, Skip the next step or Stop it. Restyle only: the same states, words, controls, Stop pop-up with its optional reason, and the same rule that the card hides itself for people without Automation access. Teal (Conversation) because the card is about messages sent to the customer. Researched against HubSpot (enrolled-in-sequence notice with Pause and Unenroll on the contact), HighLevel and Close (active and past workflows on the contact) and Jobber (automatic quote follow-ups).",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-large",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "e7NjU",
          "name": "Part 1 · Pick a look",
