    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "bM4k0",
      "x": 23284,
      "y": 360,
      "name": "Concept · Batch 61 · ⋯ menu and select · Approved B and B · 2026-10-22",
      "width": 1500,
      "fill": "$color-surface-background",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 48,
      "padding": 48,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "f5XaMl",
          "name": "Intro",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "UFQ0S",
              "name": "Eyebrow",
              "fill": "$color-interactive",
              "content": "CONCEPT · BATCH 61 · SHARED PARTS",
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-small",
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": 0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "hyPDS",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$color-heading",
              "content": "⋯ menu and select",
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-jumbo",
              "fontWeight": "700",
              "letterSpacing": -0.6
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "YFQdV",
              "name": "Lead",
              "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1100,
              "content": "Approved Menu B and Select B by Jafar 2026-10-22; Menu A (clean list) and Select A (quiet box, tick list) deleted. Two shared parts used all over the app. (1) The ⋯ menu (ui/DropdownMenu): the small list of actions that opens from a ⋯ button, a More button or an Add button. It already carries plain rows, rows with an icon, rows on a coloured tile with a quiet hint line, group headings, a footer below a divider, red delete rows, greyed rows, quiet rows that explain instead of acting, and a green tick on the current choice. (2) The select box (ui/Select): pick one value from a fixed list, with an optional label, a leading icon or word (“Status · All”), colour dots on options, greyed options, a lock when only one choice exists, and an error line. Nothing new is added to either; only the look changes. Proven patterns followed: Linear, Stripe and Notion menus (icons in one quiet colour, destructive rows last behind a divider, headings only on long menus, a tick for the current choice); Stripe and Jobber selects (white box, the chosen value with a tick, colour only where the value has a status).",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-base",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "oLI5P",
          "name": "Menu · Option B",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 20,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "vlZAp",
              "name": "Option heading",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 4,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "BV41z",
                  "name": "Option title",
                  "fill": "$color-heading",
                  "content": "Approved · Menu B · Icon squares and a danger strip · 2026-10-22",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-family",
                  "fontSize": "$font-size-large",
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "j8ZNn",
                  "name": "Option note",
                  "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 1100,
                  "content": "Each icon sits in a small grey square, so a menu reads like a tidy column of buttons; on hover the row turns grey and its square turns white. Red actions live together at the bottom on a soft red strip, so “delete” is never next to a safe action by accident. The current choice is a solid green circle with a white tick. Slightly taller rows (40) and rounder corners.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-family",
                  "fontSize": "$font-size-base",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "WRbH0",
              "name": "Stage menu B",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "fill": "$color-surface-background-subtle",
              "cornerRadius": "$radius-large",
              "stroke": "$color-border",
              "strokeWidth": 1,
              "gap": 48,
              "padding": 40,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "tIptP",
                  "name": "Column · Actions on a line · ⋯",
                  "width": 236,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 6,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "jouM9",
                      "name": "Caption",
                      "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Actions on a line",
                      "fontFamily": "$font-family",
                      "fontSize": "$font-size-small",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
