            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "UYEM1",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$color-heading",
              "content": "Branding: your logo and colour, and exactly where customers see them",
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-largest",
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "OgQmR",
              "name": "Lead",
              "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1200,
              "content": "The page behind Branding on Settings home (and the Logo in Branding link on Business profile). Logo and colour on the left, a live preview of what customers see on the right, a floating save bar once something changes. It keeps everything the live page does: upload, replace or remove the logo (PNG, JPG or WEBP up to 2 MB, checked for safety before it shows), pick the brand colour, reset to default, Save and Cancel, the read-only view for staff and the someone-saved-first message. Research: Stripe Branding, Shopify Brand, Square invoices, Jobber. Option B (brand kit) was not chosen and has been removed.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-base",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
