      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 48,
      "padding": 48,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "xRfbQ",
          "name": "Intro",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "PXX3r",
              "name": "Eyebrow",
              "fill": "$color-interactive",
              "content": "COMMUNICATIONS · STAGE 10 · NUMBER PAPERWORK · APPROVED BY JAFAR · 2026-10-22",
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-overline",
              "fontWeight": "700",
              "letterSpacing": 0.6
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "GTjFf",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$color-heading",
              "content": "Number paperwork: the documents a country asks for before you can buy a texting number there",
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-largest",
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Wwlwt",
              "name": "Lead",
              "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1200,
              "content": "Opened from Phone & SMS and from the Add number pop-up's \"Start paperwork\". The list shows every set of paperwork, one per country and number kind, with a plain status: Draft, Under review, Approved or Needs a fix. A new set is filled in four steps on its own page: country and kind, business details (filled in from the texting registration you already gave), documents, then check and send. Research: GoHighLevel's Regulatory Bundle / Address list and create flow (country → number type → business, representative and documents → submit; the reason shows on a rejected bundle), and Twilio's Regulations API (the fields and documents asked for come live from Twilio per country; statuses draft, in review, approved, rejected with a reason). US and Canada need no paperwork to buy, so they never appear here.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-base",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "bzj2R",
          "name": "Screen 1 · Paperwork list",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
