    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "nLAe4",
      "x": 5672,
      "y": 39655,
      "name": "Concept · Communications · Charges before sending · Approved B · 2026-10-22",
      "width": 1536,
      "fill": "$color-surface-background",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 48,
      "padding": 48,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "wsthi",
          "name": "Intro",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "ySBkP",
              "name": "Eyebrow",
              "fill": "$color-interactive",
              "content": "COMMUNICATIONS · STAGE 10 · CHARGES BEFORE SENDING · APPROVED B BY JAFAR · 2026-10-22",
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-overline",
              "fontWeight": "700",
              "letterSpacing": 0.6
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "zBsKD",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$color-heading",
              "content": "Charges before sending: what will this text cost, before I press Send?",
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-largest",
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "H0FDSv",
              "name": "Lead",
              "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1200,
              "content": "The inbox reply box, writing a text. Before sending, the contractor sees where the text goes and its price per segment (in the To line), how many segments it fills (blocks under the message), the whole price (on Send) and the balance (beside Send). When the balance can't cover the text, Send is off. Buying a number shows its charges on the Add number pop-up's bill (approved separately). Research: GoHighLevel and Twilio charge per segment (160 characters, or 153 each when a text is split; emoji make it 70/67) at a price per destination country; HelloSMS and SimpleTexting show a live segment counter under the message. Example: Road LTD in Burnaby, Canada. Prices are examples; real ones are Jafar's selling prices.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-base",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "B5hYEu",
          "name": "Option B · Price on the Send button",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 16,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "jiSS0",
              "name": "Label",
              "fill": "$color-heading",
              "content": "Approved B · The price is on the Send button",
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-larger",
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Hg7tI",
              "name": "Note",
              "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1200,
              "content": "The cost lives where the decision happens. Send reads \"Send · $0.33\", so the price is the last thing you see before pressing. The country and its price per segment sit in the To line, next to the customer's number. Under the message a bar fills as you type, one block per segment, so you can see a long text about to tip into another segment (and cost more) before it does. Your balance sits quietly beside Send; when it can't cover the text, a red line under the bar says so and Send is off.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-base",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "yQ7fF",
              "name": "State · At home · Tom in Canada · 1 segment",
