    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "v6Jtu",
      "x": 7368,
      "y": 39655,
      "name": "Concept · Communications · Uplift texting setup · Approved mix (B + A's table) · 2026-10-22",
      "width": 1536,
      "fill": "$color-surface-background",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 48,
      "padding": 48,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "bLhLf",
          "name": "Intro",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "bmCm4",
              "name": "Eyebrow",
              "fill": "$color-interactive",
              "content": "COMMUNICATIONS · STAGE 10 · UPLIFT'S TEXTING SETUP (JAFAR PANEL) · APPROVED MIX BY JAFAR · 2026-10-22",
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-overline",
              "fontWeight": "700",
              "letterSpacing": 0.6
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "wkeYQ",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$color-heading",
              "content": "Uplift's texting setup: which countries each business can text, what they pay, and the Twilio work only we can do",
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-largest",
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "jm3fN",
              "name": "Lead",
              "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1200,
              "content": "For Jafar and the Uplift team, in the Control Room. Today these controls are plain cards on an organization's Communications tab (SMS mode, SMS registration, SMS sender capabilities) and an \"SMS retail rates\" list under Settings. Twilio does not let software switch texting countries on, so a person turns each country on in Twilio's Geo permissions and comes back to say it's done; only then does the business see Ready. Research: GoHighLevel's agency Phone Integration table (each sub-account with its phone provider and rebilling on or off), Twilio's Geo permissions page (countries ticked per account, low and high risk kept apart) and Twilio's price list per country. Example: Road LTD in Burnaby, Canada asked to text the United Kingdom and Mexico. Prices are placeholders; the real ones are Jafar's selling prices.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-base",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "LL8zw",
          "name": "Approved · Texting setup page (B)",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 16,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "mV8vx",
              "name": "Label",
              "fill": "$color-heading",
              "content": "Approved · Texting setup page: one to-do queue for every business",
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-larger",
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "S2V8Vj",
              "name": "Note",
              "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1200,
              "content": "A new concept. Texting setup gets its own page under Platform Operations, built like an inbox: everything Uplift must do by hand, for every business, waits in one queue. Pick a task and its panel walks you through it step by step: the price, the opt-out words, the Twilio tick with a button that opens the right account, then Mark as turned on. Country prices live on the same page's Countries & prices tab. A business's own tab keeps a short summary that links here.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-family",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-base",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
