                      "name": "Why",
                      "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Ticks inside the bubble, solid white: a clock while sending, one tick when Facebook has it, two ticks when delivered, and a filled white circle with a green double tick once read. No line under the message. Hovering the ticks shows a tip (“Seen at 9:26 AM”); clicking them opens Message details with Sent, Delivered and Seen times, as WhatsApp's Message info does. Failed: a solid red circle with a white “!” sits left of the bubble (as iMessage does), and under it Facebook's reason in plain words and Retry. Changed 2026-10-23 at Jafar's request.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font-family",
                      "fontSize": 12,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
